class:: TPoissonRand
summary:: Triggered Poisson count sampler
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Distributions
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/TGeometricRand, Classes/TIRand

description::

Returns a nonnegative integer count represented as float. It uses Knuth's bounded product method below lambda 30 and Hörmann-style PTRS transformed rejection above it, with a rounded finite fallback after 64 attempts.

Like link::Classes/TIRand::, it produces discrete triggered values; unlike TIRand's uniform interval, TPoissonRand follows a Poisson count law with equal mean and variance.

subsection:: Probability mass

image::poisson-mass.png#Poisson mass functions for lambda = 1, 4, and 10, shown in muted teal, blue, and plum. The support is discrete; increasing lambda moves the center rightward and widens it by the square root of lambda.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: lambda
Nonnegative Poisson mean. Negative or non-finite values become zero.
argument:: trig
Resample on a rising edge.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local seed.
argument:: reset
Restore the seed and sample a new initial count.
argument:: mul
Output multiplier.
argument:: add
Output offset.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ TPoissonRand.kr(4, Impulse.kr(5)).poll }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar((TPoissonRand.kr(5, Impulse.kr(8)) + 1) * 120, 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

